 \section{Conclusion}
-LoopFuzz treats response-derived protocol states and LLM output as uncertain evidence for resource allocation. Its admission criteria separate code progress from IPSM novelty, gives state-only proposals bounded provisional validation, and calibrates state productivity at scheduling episodes. The response-visible interface remains useful, while independent code feedback determines its measured value.
